.TH SIMRV-VECTOR 1 "November 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv-vector \- generate and run RISC-V vector tests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simrv-vector
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simrv-vector
uses a RISC-V vector test generator and cross-toolchain to create and run vector
instruction tests with SimRV.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-simrv \fIPATH\fR
Path to the SimRV executable. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-xlen \fI32|64\fR
Select the guest register width. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-gcc \fIPATH\fR, \-\-objcopy \fIPATH\fR, \-\-nm \fIPATH\fR
Select the RISC-V compiler and binary utilities. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-work-dir \fIPATH\fR, \-\-vector-tests-dir \fIPATH\fR
Set the artifact directory and vector test source directory. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-vlen \fIBITS\fR
Set the vector register length. The default is 256 bits.
.TP
.B \-\-jobs, \-j \fIN\fR
Set the number of parallel test jobs.
.TP
.B \-\-pattern \fIREGEX\fR
Filter generated instruction names.
.TP
.B \-\-generator \fIPATH\fR, \-\-configs-dir \fIPATH\fR
Select a prebuilt generator or its configuration directory.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simrv (1)
